          level: 'B1',
          family: 'briefing',
          freshness: 'current',
          script: "Now turn to Part two. You will hear a man briefing new staff at a hotel on their first morning. First, you have some time to look at questions eleven to twenty.\nGood morning. I'm the duty manager, and this is the half hour where I tell you the things that are not in the handbook, or that are in it and get missed.\nStart with your shifts. Early is seven until three, late is three until eleven, and you will be on a rota that changes every fortnight. The rota goes up on the Thursday before it starts. If you need a day, ask before the Thursday, because after it goes up I can only swap you with somebody who agrees.\nUniform. Shirts and aprons are provided and laundered here. Shoes are yours, and they must be closed at the toe. That is a kitchen rule that we apply everywhere, because everyone crosses the kitchen at some point.\nBreaks. On an eight-hour shift you get one hour, and it is paid. Take it in the staff room on the second floor, not in the guest areas, and not at the back door, which is where people used to go and where guests can see you.\nNow, the two rules I will not bend. The first is the key cards. Yours opens the rooms on your floor and the store cupboards. It does not open the office or the cellar, and if you find that it does, tell me, because that is a mistake and not a promotion. The second is the fire doors. They are held open by magnets and they close when the alarm sounds. Do not prop them, ever, not even for two minutes while you move a trolley.\nAbout guests, one piece of advice rather than a rule. If a guest asks you something you do not know, do not guess. Say you will find out and then actually find out. Nearly every complaint I deal with started as a small wrong answer given confidently.\nFinally, pay and problems. Pay goes in on the twenty-eighth, or the Friday before if that falls at a weekend. If something is wrong with it, come to me the same day, because the payroll cut-off is the third of the month and after that a correction waits until the next run.",
